From 40fa7abd676f6705dcfa0d52f3b650c8b37c86a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:25:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scripts, e2e: check-release.sh refuses go test -c programs,
 GOFLAGS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

scripts/check-release.sh (list after M1 no. 97):

- H3: go version -m shows no safe mark of a test program that
  go test -c builds of a main package: its build information equals
  that of a production build without VCS stamp (path, mod "(devel)",
  same settings; only a non-main package gets the path suffix .test).
  Check 3 therefore searches for two functions of package testing,
  which no program of cmd/... imports: testing.tRunner (runs each
  test) and testing.MainStart (called by the main function that
  go test generates). A test program whose TestMain never calls m.Run
  holds no testing.tRunner (the linker drops it), but always
  testing.MainStart. Each mark found is refused with
  'enthält "<mark>" (Testprogramm von go test -c)'.
- H1: the search of check 3 also passes the line GOOS through grep and
  requires it where check 1 found the setting GOOS: the build
  information in the file holds "\tGOOS=", so a tr that exits with 0
  but prints nothing (or drops that part) makes the search fail.
- H4: the script sets GOFLAGS=-json=false for go. That overrides -json
  from the environment and from the go env file; an empty GOFLAGS
  would not reach the latter. Older go versions ignore the flag.
- H2: the branch "go version with status 0 and no output" is tested.

The header names the remaining limits.

TestCheckRelease (internal/e2e/release27b_test.go) additionally builds
the test program of gomail-witness with go test -c without tags
(refused for the two marks alone), the test program of a module it
writes to a temporary directory whose TestMain calls os.Exit(0) without
m.Run (refused for testing.MainStart alone), runs the production
programs with GOFLAGS=-json in the environment and in a go env file
(exit status 0), a go that exits with 0 and prints nothing, a tr that
exits with 0 and prints nothing, and a tr that prints its whole output
and then fails.

TestReleaseSwitches (internal/e2e/release28b_test.go, no. 96) collects
with go/ast every os.Getenv and os.LookupEnv in the non-test files that
only a build with gomail_test or gomail_dev compiles, and requires each
name to be in switches of the script or to match its pattern. A name
that is not a constant (a literal, a constant of the package, + of
those) fails the test, and so does, in such a file, any other selector
named Environ, Getenv, LookupEnv or ExpandEnv whatever its receiver and
whether called or not ((*exec.Cmd).Environ, os.Environ, syscall.Getenv,
Getenv of another package, a method value), and any dot import; so
does an entry of switches that does not match the pattern or that no
such file reads.

Task: docs/tasks/28-nach-m1-nacht2c.md (Paket 28B)
